Project Revision Checklist
🔴 Priority 1 — Structure & Semantics (HTML)

 Add a single, clear <h1> to each page

 Ensure full document structure exists:

 <html> tag present

 <head> and <body> properly nested

 Replace non-semantic divs with semantic elements:

 <main>

 <section>

 <article>

 <nav>

 Remove unnecessary <hgroup> usage

 Fix incorrect nesting (e.g. h3 > p)

 Replace <b> tags used for styling with:

 <strong> where meaning is importance

 <em> where meaning is emphasis

 Replace div.button with native <button>

 Audit every element and confirm its semantic purpose

🔴 Priority 2 — CSS Fundamentals & Code Quality

 Choose spaces only (no tabs) for indentation

 Re-indent entire CSS file consistently

 Remove unnecessary or duplicated CSS rules

 Refactor selectors to follow hierarchy:

 Broad element styles first

 Narrow class-based styles after

 Replace all px values with relative units:

 rem

 em

 %

 Replace directional properties with logical ones:

 margin-block

 padding-inline

 Remove any CSS property not covered in class or not fully understood

 Add comments explaining non-obvious layout decisions

🟠 Priority 3 — Typography & Readability

 Set max line length for body text (60–70ch)

 Increase vertical spacing between:

 Paragraphs

 Headings and body text

 Major sections

 Normalize spacing for h3 + p combinations

 Reduce visual dominance of blockquotes:

 Smaller type size

 Reduced padding

 Lower contrast

 Ensure consistent text alignment across:

 Headers

 Metadata

 Body content

🟠 Priority 4 — Layout & Alignment

 Define a consistent alignment system per section

 Align headers, metadata, and body text to shared vertical axes

 Remove one-off margin/padding hacks

 Use grid or flexbox intentionally (not spacing nudges)

 Check for unintentional alignment shifts across viewports

🟡 Priority 5 — Visual System & Cohesion

 Define a cohesive “retro” visual system beyond typography:

 Color palette

 Borders / frames

 Shadows or depth rules

 Apply visual rules consistently across:

 Headers

 Navigation

 Buttons

 Blockquotes / callouts

 Remove decorative elements that don’t follow system rules

 Ensure each visual motif appears in multiple places

 Confirm retro identity survives even without the pixel font

🟡 Priority 6 — UI Patterns & Affordances

 Audit borrowed UI paradigms (email / desktop UI)

 Restore expected behaviors for known patterns

 Visually differentiate:

 External links vs anchor links

 Navigation vs content links

 Add clear affordances:

 Hover states

 Focus states

 Icons where appropriate

 Ensure “things that look the same behave the same”

🟢 Priority 7 — “Return to Top” Button (System Integration)

 Introduce the button’s visual language earlier in the page

 Reuse its style for other buttons or controls

 Improve interaction animation:

 Button translates downward on click

 Shadow recedes rather than rises

 Treat the button as a reusable UI component

🟢 Priority 8 — Evidence of Understanding

 Rebuild one section entirely from scratch

 Use fewer techniques, but apply them intentionally

 Remove any “extra” properties not taught in class

 Confirm ability to explain:

 Every HTML tag choice

 Every CSS property used

 Prioritize clarity and system thinking over polish